      "writtenOn": "2023-02-17T17:16:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What I am saying is: This doesn\u0027t test the API for InlineExecutionProhibitedException -- it tests the UrlRequest API.\n\nLooking at the definition of InlineExecutionProhibitedException, it seems that it literally only contains a default constructor. When testing the exception\u0027s API, all the test should / could do is throw an InlineExecutionProhibitedException and assert on the type of exception thrown, but there is probably very little value in doing so.\n\nSo yeah, I like this approach if it provides indirect coverage.",
      "parentUuid": "f51aaa79_9f88e09b",
